&lt;h4&gt;About the role:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cresta is looking for a Senior Developer Relations Engineer to become the technical voice of our AI agent platform in the developer and partner community. This is a hands-on, hybrid role: part software engineer, part storyteller, part community builder. You&#39;ll show developers, partners, and prospective customers how to build, test, and ship real AI agents on Cresta, primarily through video, blog posts, tutorials, and workshops, and you&#39;ll bring what you learn from that community back into the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cresta&#39;s platform is enterprise-heavy (large regulated customers, complex integrations, rigorous testing and evaluation requirements), so this role needs someone who can go deep technically, not just narrate a demo. We also maintain some open-source tooling and sample projects, so comfort working in the open is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create technical content that teaches developers how to build AI agents on Cresta&lt;/strong&gt;: blog posts, written tutorials, and long- and short-form video (walkthroughs, live coding, demo breakdowns).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and maintain sample apps, code snippets, and reference integrations&lt;/strong&gt; that show best practices for building, testing, and evaluating agents on the platform, including in open-source repos where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plan and run workshops&lt;/strong&gt; for developers and partners, both virtual and in-person, that take people from zero to a working agent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent Cresta at conferences, meetups, and partner events&lt;/strong&gt;, delivering talks and demos and engaging directly with attendees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run a feedback loop with developers and partners&lt;/strong&gt;: collect what&#39;s confusing, missing, or broken in the platform and developer experience, and route it to Product and Engineering with clear, actionable detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner cross-functionally&lt;/strong&gt; with Product, Engineering, and Marketing to keep messaging and documentation aligned with what the platform can actually do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve onboarding and the first-build experience&lt;/strong&gt; for new developers and partners evaluating the platform, including getting-started guides and sandboxes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay hands-on with agent building and testing&lt;/strong&gt;: prompt engineering, tool/function calling, RAG, and evaluation, so the content you produce reflects real, current platform capability rather than marketing copy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a software engineer, ML engineer, or developer advocate, with strong technical credibility and hands-on coding ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience building and testing AI agents: LLMs, prompt engineering, agent frameworks, function calling, RAG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in Python and/or Golang/TypeScript; able to read and write real integration code (APIs, webhooks, CRMs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of developer content: blog posts, tutorials, or videos that other engineers have actually used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public speaking or workshop-facilitation experience at meetups, conferences, or customer/partner events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication; able to explain enterprise-grade technical concepts clearly to a developer audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in an enterprise context: the platform&#39;s complexity, testing rigor, and partner requirements mean you&#39;ll need patience and depth, not just a flashy demo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup mindset: able to move fast, wear multiple hats, and adapt as the DevRel function and program mature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience contributing to or maintaining open-source projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;based in the Bay Area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
